    "Keul gathered the acorns under the oaks, soaked the bitterness out of them in the stream, and found they kept the year round.",
    "Galia dug a pit by the fire, heated stones in it, laid in a whole haunch wrapped in leaves and covered it with earth: by evening it was tender right through, and from then on the band baked its big kills and its feasts in the ground.",
    "Shunyor and the others raised the camp's first earth oven.",
    "The people of Drathholt held a feast by the fire on the longest night.",
    "Shunyor pinched a little dish of clay, filled it with fat from the kills and lit a wick of moss in its lip: a light to work by after dark.",
    "Galia threw the cracked bones from a kill into the stew pot and let them simmer the day through: the broth was rich and filling, and from then on no bone was thrown away.",
    "Galia sewed a hide into a bag with a strap for the shoulder, and brought home more from every trip.",
    "Gre noticed the hares keep to their runs, and set a loop of cord across one.",
    "Gre spread an armful of dry grass under the lean-to and slept soft and deep on it.",
    "Shunyor propped a log on a notched stick trigger at a fox earth, and took the fox in it: the first pelt, soft enough to sew into a cloak.",
    "Gre bent withies into a low dome, covered it with hides and sat inside with a sick friend round stones hot from the fire, pouring water over them, until the fever ran out of them in sweat: the band's first sweat lodge.",
